{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-cart-presale-combine.liquid

  Cart-level notice for the PRE-SALE CROSSOVER case: the cart holds at
  least one pre-sale (future) physical item AND at least one in-stock
  physical item at the same time. Sets the expectation that the whole
  order is held and posted together on the drop date, so we do not have
  to email each such customer to ask.

  Renders NOTHING unless both conditions are met, so a cart with only
  pre-sale items, or only in-stock items, never sees it.

  GENERALISED, not hardcoded to any one issue. The pre-sale signal is
  the product metafield theinmag.is_pre_order (the same flag the shop
  hero, issue strip and flip-through read), set true on the upcoming
  issue each cycle and flipped false on drop day. So this fires for
  every future pre-sale automatically, with no per-cycle edit here.

  What the SITE can and cannot do (be honest): this message only sets
  the expectation. It does NOT auto-hold the order. Holding and
  combining stays a manual/tag step on Pat's end at fulfilment.

  Drop date prefers shop.metafields.theinmag.next_release_date
  (YYYY-MM-DD); falls back to "on release day".

  No render args. Reads cart directly.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign has_presale_physical = false
  assign has_instock_physical = false

  for line in cart.items
    if line.requires_shipping
      assign line_pre = line.product.metafields.theinmag.is_pre_order | default: false
      if line_pre
        assign has_presale_physical = true
      else
        assign has_instock_physical = true
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign show_combine = false
  if has_presale_physical and has_instock_physical
    assign show_combine = true
  endif

  # Expected-arrival clause. Renders the drop date from next_release_date
  # (YYYY-MM-DD) as "15 October" style inside a parenthetical, so it updates
  # itself every pre-sale cycle. Falls back to nothing (a clean date-free
  # sentence) if the metafield is ever blank.
  assign expected_clause = ''
  assign next_release = shop.metafields.theinmag.next_release_date.value
  if next_release != blank
    assign arrival_date = next_release | date: '%-d %B'
    assign expected_clause = ' (expected ' | append: arrival_date | append: ')'
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_combine -%}
  <aside class="theinmag-cart-combine" role="note" aria-label="Pre-sale delivery">
    <span class="theinmag-cart-combine__icon" aria-hidden="true">📦</span>
    <div class="theinmag-cart-combine__copy">
      <p class="theinmag-cart-combine__heading">Everything in one parcel</p>
      <p class="theinmag-cart-combine__body">
        Your cart has a pre-sale issue, so we'll post it all together when it arrives{{ expected_clause }}.
        Saves us postage, and every bit counts for a small business. Want your in-stock issue now?
        Email <a href="mailto:heyhey@theinmag.com.au">heyhey@theinmag.com.au</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </aside>
{%- endif -%}
